<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amar Sonar Bangla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">first published September <a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as আমার সোনার বাংলা</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Amar Sonar Bangla&quot; (&quot;My Golden <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>&quot;) is an ode to Mother Bengal written by the Bengali poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabindranath-tagore">Rabindranath Tagore</a>. The exact year it was composed is not known, because the original <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> was never found. Its melody is derived from &quot;Ami Kothay Pabo Tare&quot;, a song of the Baul singer Gagan Harkara, set to the rhythm cycle Dadra tala. It is linked with the first Partition of Bengal.</p></div>
